  "body": "**Stacked on #521** (#362, Tormach PathPilot probing), which adds Tormach's probe result block. It includes #521's commits until that PR merges. #521 itself is unchanged.\n\n## What changed\nA probe program reported nothing about what it measured: on success it silently wrote `G10 L20`, and the offset table was the only trace. This came up in #521's run on a real 770MX.\n- **Tormach PathPilot / LinuxCNC** (`tormach.cps` `onProbeResult`): writes `(DEBUG, PROBE <axis> ERROR #19n)` once per probed axis.\n  - It sits after that axis's tolerance check, so the value shown has passed it, and before the `G10 L20`.\n  - In a measure-only op it comes before its `(MSG, …)` / `M0`.\n  - DEBUG shows in the status display without stopping and replaces `#n` with its value (LinuxCNC G-code reference, Messages/Comments, cited in the .cps).\n- **Fanuc / Haas / Mazak:** no report. Custom macro B has only `#3000` (alarm) and `#3006` (stop with message), and DPRNT/POPEN go to an external device. A provenance comment next to `onProbeResult` says so, and output is unchanged.\n- **Sinumerik and Heidenhain:** these posts have no probe hooks yet. The decision file records the future choice: Sinumerik `MSG(\"PROBE X ERROR \"<<R190)` then `MSG()`; Heidenhain none until FN16 to `SCREEN:` is confirmed not to stop.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/575-probe-report.md`.\n\n**Golden diffs:** only the Tormach probe goldens changed. Each gains one `(DEBUG, PROBE <axis> ERROR #19n)` line after its `o90n endif`: `probe_face`, `probe_edge`, `probe_corner`, `probe_bore_centre`, `probe_bore_centre_mm` and `probe_boss_centre`. Fanuc probe goldens and all cutting goldens are byte-identical.\n\n## How tested\n- **New `probe_report` (4):**\n  - `tormach_face_reports_z_after_its_tolerance_test_and_before_g10`\n  - `tormach_corner_reports_each_axis_before_g10`\n  - `tormach_measure_only_reports_before_its_stop`\n  - `fanuc_has_no_non_stopping_message_so_writes_no_report`\n  - The three Tormach tests failed before the change.\n- **Gate:** probe_tormach 7, probe_op 12, conformance, posting, tormach_post, fanuc_post, probe_reach, heidenhain_block_form, inverted_post and all camcraft-post tests pass. Clippy is clean.\n\n## Not exercised (draft)\nSeeing the DEBUG line on the real control. That can ride with #521's remaining mm run.\n\nChangelog: Probe programs report each probed axis's measured deviation before writing the work offset: Tormach/PathPilot shows (DEBUG, PROBE <axis> ERROR #19n) without stopping; Fanuc-family controls have no non-stopping message and write none (#575)\n\nFixes #575\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
